1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,460
Audit reports say Fixed.

2
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:05,100
Almost nobody checks the code that actually runs on chain.

3
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:08,680
FixCheck checks it, one finding at a time.

4
00:00:08,733 --> 00:00:10,803
This is a real Sherlock finding.

5
00:00:10,803 --> 00:00:12,183
Sherlock runs audit contests.

6
00:00:12,183 --> 00:00:14,253
When the team ships a fix,

7
00:00:14,253 --> 00:00:18,383
Sherlock marks the finding fixed and links the pull request.

8
00:00:18,433 --> 00:00:20,603
But the fix lands in a repository.

9
00:00:20,603 --> 00:00:23,073
The contract on chain is a separate deployment.

10
00:00:23,073 --> 00:00:27,153
It can be older than the fix, or simply never replaced.

11
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,210
Here is how a check works.

12
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:30,540
Someone files a check,

13
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:33,220
and stakes that the fix is not deployed.

14
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:35,220
Every validator reads the same evidence:

15
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:37,230
the finding's section of the report,

16
00:00:37,230 --> 00:00:38,570
the merged fix commit,

17
00:00:38,570 --> 00:00:41,240
and the verified source at the deployed address.

18
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:44,250
Code compares the functions, and decides whenever it can.

19
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:46,930
A model only sees what code cannot settle.

20
00:00:46,930 --> 00:00:51,270
It must quote a line the fix added, and two runs must agree.

21
00:00:51,270 --> 00:00:52,940
Otherwise the result is inconclusive,

22
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:54,950
and everyone is refunded.

23
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:55,420
Fixed.

24
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:57,490
PoolTogether's Claimer on OP Mainnet

25
00:00:57,490 --> 00:00:59,570
was redeployed in July 2024.

26
00:00:59,570 --> 00:01:02,890
Its function is identical to the fix commit,

27
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:05,620
so code alone says fixed.

28
00:01:05,667 --> 00:01:06,427
Not fixed.

29
00:01:06,427 --> 00:01:09,067
Check six is PoolTogether's vault on Ethereum.

30
00:01:09,067 --> 00:01:11,717
It was deployed on August 19, 2024,

31
00:01:11,717 --> 00:01:14,737
after the fix was merged on June 28.

32
00:01:14,737 --> 00:01:17,387
Its function is still the audited version.

33
00:01:17,387 --> 00:01:20,717
This is the only not fixed result.

34
00:01:20,767 --> 00:01:21,817
Predates the audit.

35
00:01:21,817 --> 00:01:25,307
This vault on OP Mainnet was deployed in April 2024,

36
00:01:25,307 --> 00:01:26,347
before the audit.

37
00:01:26,347 --> 00:01:29,837
It is immutable, so it could never contain the fix.

38
00:01:29,837 --> 00:01:32,627
FixCheck does not blame the team for that.

39
00:01:32,627 --> 00:01:34,347
It says so.

40
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:35,360
Predates the fix.

41
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:37,600
Check five is the vault on Arbitrum.

42
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:39,510
It was deployed on May 29.

43
00:01:39,510 --> 00:01:41,750
The fix was merged on June 28.

44
00:01:41,750 --> 00:01:45,270
It could not contain a fix that did not exist yet,

45
00:01:45,270 --> 00:01:47,550
so every stake is refunded.

46
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:47,980
Inconclusive.

47
00:01:47,980 --> 00:01:51,000
The explorer verified this contract's source only partially,

48
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,770
so the code shown may not be exactly what runs.

49
00:01:54,770 --> 00:01:57,410
Guessing would be unfair to one side.

50
00:01:57,410 --> 00:02:01,480
Inconclusive is the honest answer, and everyone is refunded.

51
00:02:01,533 --> 00:02:04,143
Now a live check, on the demo contract,

52
00:02:04,143 --> 00:02:06,103
where the window is 90 seconds.

53
00:02:06,103 --> 00:02:07,413
Pick a real finding.

54
00:02:07,413 --> 00:02:08,383
Before you pay,

55
00:02:08,383 --> 00:02:11,983
the app runs the same checks the contract will.

56
00:02:12,033 --> 00:02:15,523
File the check, with a stake that it is not fixed.

57
00:02:15,523 --> 00:02:19,053
Every validator fetches the sources, and they must agree.

58
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:20,370
The check is open.

59
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:24,520
Until the window closes, anyone can stake that it is fixed.

60
00:02:24,567 --> 00:02:28,987
90 seconds later, anyone can ask the validators to decide.

61
00:02:29,033 --> 00:02:31,233
This vault was deployed before the audit.

62
00:02:31,233 --> 00:02:33,433
So the verdict is predates the audit,

63
00:02:33,433 --> 00:02:35,683
and every stake comes back.

64
00:02:35,733 --> 00:02:37,963
Refunds and winnings wait in your balance.

65
00:02:37,963 --> 00:02:40,213
Withdraw them whenever you like.

66
00:02:40,267 --> 00:02:43,357
Across 22 checks of 21 real findings,

67
00:02:43,357 --> 00:02:45,567
from four protocols: 7 fixed,

68
00:02:45,567 --> 00:02:48,667
1 not fixed, 6 predate the audit,

69
00:02:48,667 --> 00:02:52,417
1 predates its fix, and 7 inconclusive.

70
00:02:52,467 --> 00:02:54,707
Every verdict is contract state on GenLayer.

71
00:02:54,707 --> 00:02:57,917
You can read it yourself on the explorer.

72
00:02:57,967 --> 00:03:01,107
The code deployed at these addresses matches the repository,

73
00:03:01,107 --> 00:03:02,817
byte for byte.

74
00:03:02,867 --> 00:03:05,757
Two independent attack rounds found 21 issues.

75
00:03:05,757 --> 00:03:10,117
All of them are fixed, and 183 tests pass.

76
00:03:10,167 --> 00:03:12,417
What is not fixed yet is written down,

77
00:03:12,417 --> 00:03:15,317
in the Known limitations section of the README.

78
00:03:15,367 --> 00:03:19,687
Next time a report says Fixed, you can check.

79
00:03:19,687 --> 00:03:20,847
fixcheck-ledger.vercel.app
